                <pb facs="0141" n="131" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg131"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation (3)/100: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">White</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Port
                                au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-23T12:00:00-05:00">December 23,
                        1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>276. The Dominican Government has approached the Haitian Government for support
                    to a resolution to be proposed at Rio de Janeiro to the effect that those
                    American Governments which have not yet declared war should do so cojointly.</p>
                <pb facs="0142" n="132" xml:id="pg132"/>
                <p>The Haitian Minister for Foreign Affairs would be grateful for the Department’s
                    reactions as soon as possible. He himself has no objections to supporting such a
                    resolution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
